[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m. The project is a single static HTML page, so I used a native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">
[39m  with a placeholder "My task" label and no JavaScript. The browser handles the on/off state itself, and because it's
  wrapped in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, clicking the text toggles it too. I also added a small CSS rule that greys out and strikes
  through the text when the box is checked, so a done item looks done. Delete that [38;5;153m<style>[39m block if you want it plainer.

  I haven't opened it in a browser, and nothing is committed. The checked state also isn't saved, so it resets when the
  page reloads. That fits "nothing fancy", but if you want it to persist, saving it to [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m would take a few
  lines.

